#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179444 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44e3a595-a9ae-5d8c-9aa5-c8e3403fcb28" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials"}] :question/id #uuid "6dfde17c-e23e-5137-86cb-f8b756788f13" :question/math-academy-id "e-5669" :question/problem "Given that $n \\geq 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac {n!} {(n - 2)!}$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\nn! = n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdot (n-2)\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-2)$! that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {n!} {(n - 2)!} &= \\dfrac {n \\cdot (n - 1) \\cdot (n - 2)!} {(n - 2)!} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {n \\cdot (n - 1) \\cdot \\cancel{(n - 2)!}} {\\cancel{(n - 2)!}} \\\\[5pt] &= n(n -1) \\\\[5pt] &= n^2 - n \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179445 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "644b7f09-7f66-50f2-8eba-ef6e009429d0" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials"}] :question/id #uuid "357d19f9-977d-5143-a881-3ecbc068556c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5670" :question/problem "Given that $k \\geq 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac {k^2(k - 1)!} {k!}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that\n\n$$\nk! = k \\cdot (k-1)\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the numerator as follows:\n\n$$\nk^2 (k-1)! = k \\cdot \\underbrace{k \\cdot (k-1)!}_{k!} = k \\cdot k\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $k$! that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {k^2(k - 1)!} {k!} &= \\dfrac {k \\cdot k!} {k!} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {k \\cdot \\cancel{k!}} {\\cancel{k!}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {k} {1} \\\\[5pt] &= k \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/id #uuid "bcdea8ab-4c41-5d45-b62f-a1f2dc9f83e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9520" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(k+1)$! for any $k \\geq 2$?\n\n1. $(k+1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k-1)$\n2. $(k+1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k-1)$!\n3. $(k+1) \\cdot k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have\n\n$$\n(k+1)! = (k+1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(k + 1)! &= (k + 1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k - 1) \\cdot (k - 2) \\cdot ⋯ \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1^(⏞)^((k - 1)!) \\\\\n&= (k + 1) \\cdot k \\cdot (k - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44e3a595-a9ae-5d8c-9aa5-c8e3403fcb28" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bca3db6d-c5c1-5f7d-92fc-cc4ceb7586cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k(k+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257461} {:answer/id #uuid "d08aad34-ac2d-5fdd-9ff8-ea9e5d1ceb98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k(k+1)(k+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257462} {:answer/id #uuid "da27039f-cd4a-5922-b5be-9f0c9a1ec7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+1)(k+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257463} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3a2ccb-3f1f-546f-ad54-e9b6ad017387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{k(k+1)(k+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257464} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6d7373-1583-55db-bb75-706c41837842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(k+1)(k+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d08aad34-ac2d-5fdd-9ff8-ea9e5d1ceb98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k(k+1)(k+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257462} :answer-field/id #uuid "82f048d7-bf0c-5242-b17c-f6e97018bc83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3757b1fa-bff3-5ebf-aae8-87bbb8f2ea11" :question/math-academy-id "q-122052" :question/problem "Given that $k\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(k+2)!}{(k-1)!}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(k+2)!=(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)\\cdot k\\cdot (k-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(k-1)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(k+2)!}{(k-1)!} & =\\frac{(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)\\cdot k\\cdot (k-1)!}{(k-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)\\cdot k\\cdot \\cancel{(k-1)!}}{\\cancel{(k-1)!}} \\\\  & =k(k+1)(k+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "644b7f09-7f66-50f2-8eba-ef6e009429d0" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e209561-4b0a-557c-802f-0a5efd206604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257468} {:answer/id #uuid "0a472835-c516-5910-805b-f7805cb08c00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257469} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2ee58b-07ea-5f37-926f-1986ccb81d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257470} {:answer/id #uuid "629819e6-148e-5cb1-adf8-947e6d73b7dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n(n-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257471} {:answer/id #uuid "ed37c071-0dab-5bae-9533-39575192858a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-1)^{2}(n-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa2ee58b-07ea-5f37-926f-1986ccb81d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257470} :answer-field/id #uuid "e312be77-589a-5e40-87c8-4626331f81a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257467}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3768b9a9-d6ba-5788-9af2-24549ab90243" :question/math-academy-id "q-122063" :question/problem "Given that $n\\ge 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\,(n-1)!}{(n-2)!}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-1)! & =(n-1)(n-2)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $(n-2)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\cdot (n-1)!}{(n-2)!} & =\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!}{(n-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\cdot (n-1)\\cancel{(n-2)!}}{\\cancel{(n-2)!}} \\\\  & =(n-1)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c90e64f6-b971-583a-a9f2-0f2e6b238c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k + 2) \\cdot k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177575} {:answer/id #uuid "192eb793-0884-5285-9d42-add055458c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177576} {:answer/id #uuid "199f723d-c8af-5880-b07a-b0c19d909d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k + 2) \\cdot (k + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177577} {:answer/id #uuid "371aa547-6f1e-54dc-a525-5e9100c066d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177578} {:answer/id #uuid "482520d9-aef7-5737-a828-3b1c8d889e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(k + 2) \\cdot k$!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192eb793-0884-5285-9d42-add055458c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177576} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8a8d747-42f1-5ad3-b02f-15d11d4b7168" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177574}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06937889-7753-54db-a2ad-60dda70867ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-124142" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(k + 2)$! for any $k \\ge 0$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7c31701-e6cc-5cb1-817d-35a2b1c78231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257661} {:answer/id #uuid "4058f54f-8bd8-5a0d-9f06-c4f3defccdcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257662} {:answer/id #uuid "740ce852-d22c-5e0a-a994-5bd0af7b2ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257663} {:answer/id #uuid "8361e86a-95c6-50c6-a121-fe5c076efb87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257664} {:answer/id #uuid "b229ae06-a681-5877-85a9-7ead2a40afdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b229ae06-a681-5877-85a9-7ead2a40afdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257665} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81ce965-92b6-5a22-89ae-97cf7e65a014" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257660}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b29e44ae-a5ba-5626-8819-be052caaf1f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124489" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(n-4)!$ for any $n\\ge 5?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have\n\n$$\n(n-4)!=(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)\\cdot (n-6)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-4)! & =(n-4)\\cdot \\overset{(n-5)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(n-5)\\cdot (n-6)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)!\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c9e9a11-582b-5642-abc1-e0e9e2083735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-2)\\cdot (n-4)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257668} {:answer/id #uuid "98026112-288f-5503-a229-829433cfd2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257669} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd1f146-2552-52bc-b334-8b349e7466b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257670} {:answer/id #uuid "3c02fb37-5681-57d8-ae4b-1a889a63578f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257671} {:answer/id #uuid "11fbcafb-2e83-5b94-bba5-8d6cc09697ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c02fb37-5681-57d8-ae4b-1a889a63578f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257671} :answer-field/id #uuid "533e9597-0fd9-5bfe-82f6-85bd0bdf80be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257667}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e61051d8-ea2b-5702-bf82-3dab92879c9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124492" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(n-2)!$ for any $n\\ge 4?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have\n\n$$\n(n-2)!=(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)\\cdot (n-5)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-2)! & =(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot \\overset{(n-4)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)!\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec1a423d-00ae-5c18-b176-f6564918ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257675} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbfd842-2bd3-5d73-a317-4d7d71c5608d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+3)\\cdot (n+1)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257676} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5bf00b-17e6-5bda-9736-dc067b0bef91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257677} {:answer/id #uuid "dd27a54b-d59e-5618-9e13-1b28c5c7a7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+2)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257678} {:answer/id #uuid "f8153453-717a-5fa9-bdcd-0cb27d0e8fa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec1a423d-00ae-5c18-b176-f6564918ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257675} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79e6af0-433a-53d2-9e69-bef7522f0bfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257674}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71c74243-2d3a-5a86-b262-41a397c01a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124498" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(n+3)!$ for any $n\\ge -1?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have\n\n$$\n(n+3)!=(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n+3)! & =(n+3)\\cdot \\overset{(n+2)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)!\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "745c18ba-b4b2-5ca2-b01b-f674d042bf96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+6)\\cdot (n+5)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257682} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc665a8-0d4b-52ee-8146-081448b0b6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+6)\\cdot (n+4)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257683} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd3b879-c086-5ba1-b450-6fce908c41c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+5)\\cdot (n+4)\\cdot (n+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257684} {:answer/id #uuid "b64b5da1-db41-598c-a0fb-ea377f30778f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(n+5)\\cdot (n+4)!" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218